{"markdown":"S\n\ne\n\ne\n\nt\n\nh\n\ne\n\np\n\no\n\ne\n\nm\n\ns\n\nLoading\n\nAccess David's library to discover his poems, essays, courses and short films\n\n[Three Sundays Series - LETTING GO - Live and Recorded](https://davidwhyte.com/store/three-sundays/jul-2026-series/)\n\n[David Whyte](https://davidwhyte.com/)\n\n[Home](https://davidwhyte.com/)\n\n[Three Sundays](https://davidwhyte.com/three-sundays-overview/)\n\nJoin David live\n\n[David Whyte\\\\\n\\\\\nCompanion Portal](https://davidwhyte.com/experience/)\n\nDavid's complete archive\n\n[Sign in](https://davidwhyte.com/account/)\n\nSubscribe\n\nSubscribe\n\n[Back to overview](https://davidwhyte.com/account/)\n\n[Back to Three Sundays](https://davidwhyte.com/courses/)\n\n[Back to talks](https://davidwhyte.com/talks/)\n\n[Back to films](https://davidwhyte.com/films/)\n\n[Poetry & Prose](https://davidwhyte.com/poetry-prose/) [Walking Tours](https://davidwhyte.com/walking-tours/) [Events & Retreats](https://davidwhyte.com/events/) [Speaking](https://davidwhyte.com/speaking/) [Invitas](https://www.invitas.net/) [Store\\\\\n\\\\\nStore](https://davidwhyte.com/store/)\n\n[Sign in](https://davidwhyte.com/account/)\n\nSubscribe\n\nSubscribe\n\n[My Three Sundays](https://davidwhyte.com/account/?tab=courses)\n\nClose\n\n[Login](https://davidwhyte.com/account/) Cart\n\n\n[David Whyte](https://davidwhyte.com/)\n\nHome [Three Sundays](https://davidwhyte.com/three-sundays-overview/) [David Whyte\\\\\n\\\\\nCompanion Portal](https://davidwhyte.com/experience/)\n\n- [Poetry & Prose](https://davidwhyte.com/poetry-prose/)\n- [Walking Tours](https://davidwhyte.com/walking-tours/)\n- [Events & Retreats](https://davidwhyte.com/events/)\n- [Speaking](https://davidwhyte.com/speaking/)\n- [Invitas](https://www.invitas.net/)\n\n- [Overview](https://davidwhyte.com/three-sundays-overview/)\n- [My Three Sundays](https://davidwhyte.com/account/?tab=courses)\n\n- [Maps](https://davidwhyte.com/maps/)\n- [Library](https://davidwhyte.com/poems-essays/)\n\n[Store](https://davidwhyte.com/store/)\n\nBackBack\n\nYou start\n\nwith a painter’s hand\n\nworking up color\n\nfrom a dark palette\n\nof remembrance\n\n(from “The Painter’s Hand”)\n\nWhat you can plan\n\nis too small\n\nfor you to live.\n\nTime to go into the dark\n\nwhere the night has eyes\n\nto recognize its own.\n\nThere you can be sure\n\nyou are not beyond love.\n\nThe dark will be your home\n\ntonight.\n\n(from “Sweet Darkness”)\n\nDespair takes us in when we\n\nhave nowhere else to go;\n\nwhen we feel the heart\n\ncannot break anymore, when\n\nour world or our loved ones\n\ndisappear, when we feel we\n\ncannot be loved or do not\n\ndeserve to be loved, when\n\nour God disappoints, or\n\nwhen our body is carrying\n\nprofound pain in a way\n\nthat does not seem to go away.\n\n(from “Despair”)\n\nYou start\n\nwith a painter’s hand\n\nworking up color\n\nfrom a dark palette\n\nof remembrance\n\n(from “The Painter’s Hand”)\n\nWhat you can plan\n\nis too small\n\nfor you to live.\n\nTime to go into the dark\n\nwhere the night has eyes\n\nto recognize its own.\n\nThere you can be sure\n\nyou are not beyond love.\n\nThe dark will be your home\n\ntonight.\n\n(from “Sweet Darkness”)\n\nDespair takes us in when we\n\nhave nowhere else to go;\n\nwhen we feel the heart\n\ncannot break anymore, when\n\nour world or our loved ones\n\ndisappear, when we feel we\n\ncannot be loved or do not\n\ndeserve to be loved, when\n\nour God disappoints, or\n\nwhen our body is carrying\n\nprofound pain in a way\n\nthat does not seem to go away.\n\n(from “Despair”)\n\nScroll to explore\n\n## Become a companion to David Whyte's work\n\nAn online archive of a lifetime's work, talks and films. There will be a pipeline of new material added to the Companion site as they become available.\n\n## Subscriber Benefits\n\n### Poetry and essays\n\n### The complete collection of David's published poetry and essays.\n\n### Video and talks\n\n### A rich archive of talks and online sessions, including a selection of Three Sundays Series.\n\n### Maps\n\n### An interactive map experience to explore the literary landscapes of David's life.\n\nAnnual Offer with One Week Free Trial [Subscribe - $75 / year](https://davidwhyte.com/register/membership/)\n\nGift David Whyte Companion Subscription [Gift - $75 / year](https://davidwhyte.com/register/annual-membership-gift/)\n\n## Commonly     Asked     Questions\n\n### Is there a monthly subscription available for the Companion?\n\nClose\n\nView\n\nCurrently, we only offer annual (12 month) subscriptions to the David Whyte Companion.\n\n### I already subscribe to David's Substack - what is the difference between that and the Companion?\n\nClose\n\nView\n\nDavid publishes twice weekly on davidwhyte.substack.com, where he selects published work from his archive, and also shares new, newly revised and not yet published poems and essays. In addition to publishing his writing, David offers personal insights into the inspiration for his writing, and will often comment on reader’s responses to his posts.\n\nPaid Substack subscribers receive exclusive discounts on new work, Three Sundays Series, and early access to register for events, retreats and walking tours.\n\nWhile David’s Substack publication is a curated collection, the David Whyte Companion portal offers members the ability to explore David’s complete published archive of poems and essays on their own. As well, the Companion Library includes a selection of short films, audio talks, recordings of David reading some of his most beloved poems and essays, and a subset of past Three Sundays Series.\n\nCompanion members can save their favorite poems, series, and talks, and access them any time in their account.\n\n### Can I gift a Companion membership to someone?\n\nClose\n\nView\n\nYes, you can gift a Companion membership to a friend or family member.  Gift subscriptions provide a free 12-month membership. Gift subscriptions to do not automatically renew when the subscription period ends.\n\nYou can purchase a David Whyte Companion gift subscription [here](https://davidwhyte.com/register/annual-membership-gift/):\n\n### When will more Three Sundays Series be added?\n\nClose\n\nView\n\nThe Three Sundays Series from 2020 – 2022 are now available in the Companion Library. Additional sessions will be added during the coming year.\n\n### I am having trouble with my subscription - who do I contact?\n\nClose\n\nView\n\nFor any questions on how to become a Companion subscriber, or for help with your account – including email, password and payment questions – contact support@davidwhyte.com and someone will be happy to assist you.\n\nShare the experience\n\nCompanion Portal\n\nDavid Whyte\n\nRestart the experience\n\nDavid Whyte Experience by received the Site of the Month on [Awwwards](https://www.awwwards.com/sites/david-whyte-experience) and the Site of the Day on [Awwwards](https://www.awwwards.com/sites/david-whyte-experience), [CSS](https://www.cssdesignawards.com/sites/david-whyte-experience/46739/) and [FWA](https://thefwa.com/cases/david-whyte-experience-p2).\n\n\n[Poetry & Prose](https://davidwhyte.com/poetry-prose/) [Walking Tours](https://davidwhyte.com/walking-tours/) [Events](https://davidwhyte.com/events/)\n\nInvitas\n\nThe Institute for Conversational Leadership\n\n[Discover Invitas](https://www.invitas.net/)\n\nGet in touch\n\nA member of our team will get back to you.\n\nCONTACT US\n\n[Speaking Engagements](https://davidwhyte.com/speaking/) [Permission Inquiries](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1srlNufVdl9GeRuY7lZ8hs9CsO50muCu1YbYyRI0OiFI/viewform?edit_requested=true#response=ACYDBNg_zD[%E2%80%A6]GZugtd9o78wXHObP9WmI) [About Many Rivers](https://davidwhyte.com/about-many-rivers/)\n\nCopyright 2026\n\n[Privacy Policy](https://davidwhyte.com/privacy-policy/) [Terms & Conditions](https://davidwhyte.com/terms-conditions/)\n\nClose\n\nGet in touchContact Us\n\nYour message\n\nhCaptcha\n\n![Check mark](<Base64-Image-Re